 1, 41", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "lamenting, weeping, MBh. &c.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "‘a friend or protector’ [only neg. अन्-आक्रन्द mf(आ)n. ‘not having on whom to call for help’, ‘without a protector’, MBh. i, 6568; iii, 13859]", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "a king who is the friend of a neighbouring king and checks the attack made on him by another king (called पार्ष्णि-ग्राह, q.v.), Mn. vii, 207; VarBṛS.; Kām.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "(= संग्राम) war, battle, Naigh.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["आक्रंदः", "आक्रन्दः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["AkraMdaH", "AkrandaH"]}], "akrandana": [{"id": "Akrandana", "headword": "आक्रन्दन", "headword_slp1": "Akrandana", "fold": "akrandana", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "आ-क्रन्दन n. lamentation, Pañcat.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["आक्रंदनं"], "synonyms_slp1": ["AkraMdanaM"]}], "akrandaniya": [{"id": "AkrandanIya", "headword": "आक्रन्दनीय", "headword_slp1": "AkrandanIya", "fold": "akrandaniya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "आ-क्रन्दनीय mfn. to be called for help, Kathās.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "akrandika": [{"id": "Akrandika", "headword": "आक्रन्दिक", "headword_slp1": "Akrandika", "fold": "akrandika", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "आक्रन्दिक mf(ई)n. running to where cries for help are heard, Pāṇ. iv, 4, 38.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["आक्रंदिक"], "synonyms_slp1": ["AkraMdika"]}], "akrandin": [{"id": "Akrandin", "headword": "आक्रन्दिन्", "headword_slp1": "Akrandin", "fold": "akrandin", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "आ-क्रन्दिन् mfn. ifc. invoking in a weeping tone, Kum. v, 26.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["आक्रंदिन्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["AkraMdin"]}], "akram": [{"id": "Akram", "headword": "आक्रम्", "headword_slp1": "Akram", "fold": "akram", "headword_language": "sa",